meta {
  name: Export
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

get {
  url: {{newBase}}/competitions/{{compId}}/export
  body: none
  auth: none
}

vars:post-response {
  exportEtag: res.headers.etag
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  The whole competition in one request: `classes`, `runners`, `results`.

  **What only this endpoint has:**

  - `runners[].id` — stable per-competition runner ids. `classresults` has no id
    field at all, which is why the plan ties the result-identity change to adopting
    export.
  - `classes[].radioControls` — `{ code, name }` before anyone has punched.
  - `relayLeg` + `relayClassName` — relay legs grouped, with the team name as club.

  **What it lacks:** `place`, `timeplus`, `progress`, and per-split `place` /
  `timeplus`. Result rows are just
  `{ runnerId, control, time, status, changed }`. So it is a change-detection oracle,
  not a replacement for `classresults`.

  Try it with and without `Accept-Encoding: gzip, br` (see quirks/Brotli): 343 KB
  raw against 35 KB compressed on this competition.
}
